# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form delivery (browser side)
#
# Where the contact form POSTs to. Any endpoint that accepts a JSON body works
# — Formspree, Basin, a Cloudflare Worker, your own API. The payload:
#
#   { "form": "contact", "name": "...", "email": "...", "message": "..." }
#
# Leave it unset and the form falls back to opening the visitor's mail client
# with everything pre-filled, so a message still reaches info@hinit.nl.
#
# VITE_ variables are baked into the public bundle — never put a secret here.
VITE_FORM_ENDPOINT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Appointment booking (server side — the Vercel functions in /api)
#
# The picker reads free/busy from, and books into, the owner's Google
# Calendar. These are secrets: set them in the Vercel project (Settings →
# Environment Variables) for Production and Preview. For `vercel dev` put
# them in .env.local (git-ignored). Mint the refresh token once with
# `npm run auth:google` — see README, "Google Calendar".
#
# These are OAuth credentials, not an API key: a Calendar API key (AIza...)
# only reads calendars that are public to everyone and can never create an
# event, so it cannot run this. Verify a set with `npm run check:google`.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# which calendar: "primary" or a calendar's ID from its settings page
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID=primary
